# Quality benchmark

This repo ships a **voice-first driver assistant**. Every non-trivial change must meet the bar below. Skills: `requirements-gate` (before coding), `dev-workflow` (end-to-end), `bug-fix` (regression test first).

## 1. Requirements quality

Before writing code (`requirements-gate`):

- **No silent guesses** on unhappy paths, API contract, scope, cross-service impact, or business rules.
- **One-line scope + assumptions** stated, or one focused question — then implement.
- **Contract first** when adding/changing HTTP routes, tool schemas, or store shapes consumed by another service/app.
- **Lang split**: behavior in `voicebot/vn/` and `voicebot/en/` must stay mirrored unless the task is explicitly single-lang.

**Bar:** A reviewer can predict behavior on success, empty, error, and timeout without reading the diff twice.

## 2. Code quality

Follow stack rules (do not invent parallel patterns):

| Area | Rule file |
|------|-----------|
| Layout / boundaries | `project-structure.mdc`, `service-layer.mdc` |
| TS backends | `typescript-backend.mdc` |
| Voice agent | `python-voice-agent.mdc` |
| Mobile UI | `ui-mobile.mdc` |

**Bar:**

- One concern per file; no duplicate logic across vn/en or web/mobile.
- Service boundaries: voice-agent → trip-service via HTTP only — no direct DB from Python.
- Early returns, typed boundaries, no secrets in git, no debug `print`/`console.log` left behind.
- Smallest correct diff — no drive-by refactors.

## 3. Testing quality

**When tests are required:** bug fixes (regression test that failed before fix), non-trivial logic, parsers/formatters, store reducers, tool handlers, DEV log formatters.

**When to skip:** pure copy/style, config-only, or changes covered by an existing test — say so in the report.

| Project | Minimum verify |
|---------|----------------|
| `src/backend/<ts-service>` | `npm run build` (`ops-service`: also `npm run verify:ops`) |
| `src/backend/voice-agent` | relevant `pytest tests/…` (add test for new behavior) |
| Vite frontends | `typecheck` / `build` / `lint` per app |
| `driver-app` / `customer-app` | `npm run verify` where present; exercise changed UI on device/simulator when visual |

**Bar:** Tests assert **behavior**, not implementation details. A bug fix includes a test that would fail on the old code.

## 4. Logging quality

Every line is grep-friendly. Callers pass **facts** (`get_logger` / `getLogger` + `bind`); **shape** is owned by `services/logger`:

```
{ts} {LEVEL} {service} {fn} room={room} conv={conv} — {msg} k=v
```

`room` / `conv` are always present (`-` when unknown). Concurrent sessions: `grep 'room=driver-…'`. Pipeline traces still include `DEV `:

```
DEV ok=true|false event=<kind> key=value duration_ms=…
```

| Layer | Module |
|-------|--------|
| voice-agent | `app/services/logger` (formatter on all stdlib logs after `bind` in `session.py`); `app/devlog.py` for pipeline events |
| trip-service, auth-service, call-center, call-logger, ops-service | `src/services/logger` + `attachLogContext` middleware |
| driver-app | `src/services/logger` + `devlog.ts` (`__DEV__` only) |

**Rules:**

- `ok=false` + `error`/`detail` on failures; `duration_ms` on I/O and pipeline steps.
- Event names: stable `snake_case` (`http`, `tool`, `voice_connect`, `turn`, …).
- No PII/secrets/tokens/full phone numbers in extra fields (`room` already identifies the session).
- Prefer `get_logger` / `devlog.event` over ad hoc `console.log`.

**Bar:** `grep 'room=<id>'` (or `grep 'DEV '`) reconstructs one failed user session without mixing concurrent callers.

## 5. Monitoring & observability

**Voice latency** (`turn_metrics.py`): speech-to-first-audio ≥ **2s** is **SLOW** — log and investigate.

Emit DEV/metrics on:

- HTTP to trip-service (status, duration)
- Tool calls (name, ok, duration)
- LiveKit connect/disconnect, STT final, turn timings (EOU, LLM TTFT, TTS TTFB)
- Prefetch / context warm paths

**Bar:** A production incident can be narrowed to STT vs LLM vs TTS vs backend HTTP from logs alone.

## 6. Render & UI quality

Mobile (`driver-app`, `customer-app`): **`ui-mobile.mdc`** — Screen shell, Tamagui tokens, AppText scale, 44pt, layout constants, anti-patterns, verify checklist.

Web (`driver-web`, `customer-web`, `admin-panel`): **`ui-web.mdc`** — WCAG 2.2 AA, MUI 8px grid, palette tokens, layout shells, 44px touch, anti-patterns, verify checklist.

**Bar:**

- Readable in light + dark; no hardcoded brand hex in screens.
- Map/chat overlays clear tab bar and floating assistant button.
- Web previews of RN components are approximate — **device/simulator** is authoritative for pixels.

## 7. Voice & chat response quality

**Accuracy over fluency:** tools and prompts must not invent trip data — use `context_store`, trip-service, and tool results.

**UX:**

- One chat bubble per utterance; grow with STT chunks; lock on final transcript.
- Assistant orb reflects session state (idle mic → connected waves).
- Errors: spoken + UI message in driver language (vn/en), not raw stack traces.

**Latency budget:** optimize prefetch, warm LLM, and tool round-trips before adding client complexity.

**Bar:** Driver can complete confirm trip / check upcoming / navigate flow by voice without touching the screen for the happy path.

## 8. Agent report quality (AI output to user)

When finishing a task:

- State **what changed** and **what was verified** (commands run, devices used).
- Say explicitly what was **not** verified and why.
- No false “done” — if tests weren’t run, say so.
- Vietnamese, concise, complete sentences — no telegram lists of identifiers.

## Definition of done (all must pass)

- [ ] Requirements gate passed (assumptions stated or questions answered)
- [ ] Code matches stack rules and service boundaries
- [ ] Verify commands run for every touched project
- [ ] New behavior has meaningful test coverage where applicable
- [ ] DEV logs added/updated for new I/O or failure modes
- [ ] UI/voice changes checked on target platform when feasible
- [ ] Second Brain updated if a durable decision/pattern emerged
